Zizzix the gnome crouched behind a fern in Stranglethorn Vale, his succubus Aelith shimmering beside him. A patrol of Bloodscalp trolls marched past. "Seduce the big one," Zizzix whispered. Aelith blew a kiss; the troll froze, dazed. Zizzix nuked him down, then the next. Easy. But when a raptor pack ambushed them, Aelith's Lash of Pain tickled while the raptors chewed Zizzix's ankles. He died twice. Later, a quest mob resisted Seduction entirely. Zizzix sighed. "You're great for single targets," he told Aelith, "but I keep needing a bodyguard." He summoned a voidwalker instead. It was uglier, slower, and did less damage—but it held aggro, ate shadows, and sacrificed itself to shield him. In STV, survival beat style.

**Answer:** Voidwalkers are the default because they're the only pet that can tank and keep threat, letting warlocks survive elite quests and group content. Succubus is better for solo leveling (Seduction + Lash of Pain), but most warlocks level in groups or need survivability, so they run voidwalkers out of habit and safety. [end of text]


